{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a100000000000001",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -700,
      "width": 5180,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n# Martingales and stopping times\n\nStart with what is known, then conditional means, then decisions to stop. Open a linked card for the complete definition, proof and assumptions. Arrows state a mathematical relationship.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n鞅与停时：先分清已知信息，再讨论条件均值，最后处理停止规则。点击双链阅读完整定义、证明与条件；箭头说明数学关系。"
    },
    {
      "id": "a100000000000002",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -340,
      "width": 5180,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## 1 · Information\n\nWhat is known now, and what must be known before the next step?\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n1 · 信息结构：当前知道什么？哪些量必须提前一期确定？",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a101000000000001",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[滤过定义|Filtration]]\n\nAn increasing family $(\\mathcal F_t)$ of sigma-algebras on the same outcomes records which events are known by time $t$. Information is retained; independence is not required.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一结果空间上递增的σ代数族，记录到时刻 $t$ 已知的事件。信息不会丢失；不要求独立。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a101000000000002",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[自然滤过|Natural filtration]]\n\nThe raw history $\\mathcal F_t^X=\\sigma(X_s:s\\le t)$ is the smallest filtration making $X$ adapted. The present value alone may forget earlier observations.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n原始自然滤过由截至当前的完整历史生成，是使过程适应的最小滤过。仅看当前值可能遗忘过去。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a101000000000003",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[适应过程|Adapted process]]\n\nEach $X_t$ is measurable with respect to the information $\\mathcal F_t$ available then. Adaptation imposes neither finite expectations nor a conditional-mean restriction.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n每个当前值 $X_t$ 都对当时信息 $\\mathcal F_t$ 可测。适应性本身不保证可积，也不规定条件均值。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a101000000000004",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[适应不推鞅|Adaptation and the martingale property]]\n\nBeing observable now does not make the next conditional change mean-zero. Enlarging the filtration preserves adaptation but can change the martingale property.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n当前可观测不保证下一步条件增量均值为零。扩大滤过仍保持适应，却可能改变鞅性质。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a101000000000005",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2700,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[离散可预测过程|Discrete predictable process]]\n\nFor integer $n\\ge1$, $H_n$ is $\\mathcal F_{n-1}$-measurable: its value is determined before step $n$. This is stronger than adaptation; the initial value is specified separately.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n整数 $n\\ge1$ 时，$H_n$ 对上一期信息可测，即本步之前已能确定。它比适应更强，初值另行规定。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a100000000000003",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 560,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## 2 · Conditional means\n\nThe restriction concerns the mean given current information, not the direction of every path.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n2 · 条件均值：约束给定当前信息的平均方向，不要求每条路径沿该方向移动。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000001",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[鞅差序列|Martingale differences]]\n\nReal, adapted, integrable differences $D_n$, $n\\ge1$, satisfy $E[D_n\\mid\\mathcal F_{n-1}]=0$ a.s. They need not be independent.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实值、适应、可积的增量 $D_n$，给定上一期信息的条件均值为零。各增量不必独立。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000009",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[鞅差部分和|Partial sums of martingale differences]]\n\nWith integrable, $\\mathcal F_0$-measurable $M_0$, set $M_n=M_0+\\sum_{k=1}^nD_k$. These finite sums form a martingale for the same filtration.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n加上可积且在初始信息下已知的 $M_0$，再累积鞅差，所得有限部分和相对于同一滤过为鞅。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000002",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[鞅定义|Martingales]]\n\nReal, adapted to the specified filtration, and $E|X_t|<\\infty$ at each time. For every fixed $s\\le t$, $E[X_t\\mid\\mathcal F_s]=X_s$ a.s.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n未来的条件均值等于当前值；必须连同给定滤过一起陈述。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000003",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[次鞅|Submartingales]]\n\nReal, adapted to the specified filtration, and $E|X_t|<\\infty$ at each time. For every fixed $s\\le t$, $E[X_t\\mid\\mathcal F_s]\\ge X_s$ a.s.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n未来的条件均值不小于当前值；不要求路径单调上升。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000004",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2700,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[超鞅|Supermartingales]]\n\nReal, adapted to the specified filtration, and $E|X_t|<\\infty$ at each time. For every fixed $s\\le t$, $E[X_t\\mid\\mathcal F_s]\\le X_s$ a.s.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n未来的条件均值不大于当前值；不要求路径单调下降。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000005",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Doob分解|Discrete Doob decomposition]]\n\nA real discrete-time submartingale splits as $X_n=M_n+A_n$: $M$ is a martingale and $A$ is integrable, predictable and nondecreasing. Setting $A_0=0$ makes the decomposition unique.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实值离散次鞅分为鞅与可积、可预测、非递减过程之和。固定 $A_0=0$ 才有唯一性，无需二阶矩。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000006",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[恒定均值不推鞅|Constant means and conditional fairness]]\n\nA martingale has constant unconditional means. The converse fails: opposing drifts in different information states can cancel in the overall average.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n鞅的无条件均值保持不变，反向推理不成立：不同信息状态下的相反漂移可能在总体平均中抵消。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000007",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2700,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凸变换产生次鞅|Convex transforms of martingales]]\n\nFor a real martingale $M$, finite convex $\\varphi:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ gives a submartingale with respect to the same filtration if $E|\\varphi(M_t)|<\\infty$ at every time.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n条件Jensen给出方向；逐时点可积性不可省略，结论相对于同一滤过。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a102000000000008",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[恒均值次鞅即鞅|Constant-mean submartingales]]\n\nA submartingale with constant finite means is a martingale for the same filtration. Its nonnegative conditional expected gains have mean zero, so they vanish almost surely.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一滤过下，次鞅若各期有限均值恒定，就是鞅：非负条件期望增益的均值为零，只能几乎必然消失。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a100000000000004",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1660,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## 3 · Random stopping\n\nCheck the stopping rule, then distinguish a fixed finite cutoff from a random terminal value.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n3 · 随机停止：先检验规则，再分清固定有限截断与随机终值。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "a100000000000005",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4290,
      "y": 640,
      "width": 200,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n**Stopping a martingale**\n\nConditional fairness + observable stopping.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n**停止鞅**\n\n条件公平性与可观测停止规则结合。",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000001",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[停时定义|Stopping time]]\n\nFor every finite time $t$, $\\{T\\le t\\}\\in\\mathcal F_t$: whether stopping has occurred is decidable then. Discrete and continuous time allow $0$ and $\\infty$; finiteness is not automatic.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n每个有限时刻，都能用当时信息判断是否已停。离散与连续时间均允许 $0$ 和 $\\infty$；定义不保证最终必停。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000002",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[离散首次到达停时|Discrete first entrance]]\n\nFor an adapted discrete process and a fixed measurable target $A$, $T=\\inf\\{n\\ge0:X_n\\in A\\}$ is a stopping time by a finite union of past events. No hit gives $\\infty$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n离散适应过程首次进入固定可测目标的时刻是停时，证明用有限个过去事件的并集。起点在目标内则为 $0$，不命中则为 $\\infty$。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000003",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[末次到达通常非停时|Last visits and future information]]\n\nA last-visit rule can distinguish paths with identical observations so far, even with a fixed finite horizon. Its status depends on the model and filtration; special cases can be stopping times.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n即使固定有限期限，末访规则仍可能区分当前历史相同的路径。是否为停时取决于模型与滤过，特殊情形可以成立。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000004",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2700,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[停时信息集|Information at a stopping time]]\n\nIn discrete or continuous time, $A\\in\\mathcal F_T$ means $A\\in\\mathcal F$ and $A\\cap\\{T\\le t\\}\\in\\mathcal F_t$ at every time t.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n到停止时已知的事件形成同一个 σ 代数。离散时间可按 {T=n} 分支检验；连续时间保留 {T≤t} 条件。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000012",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4500,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[停时信息单调性|Ordered stopping-time information]]\n\nFor stopping times of the same filtration, pointwise $S\\le T$ gives $\\mathcal F_S\\subseteq\\mathcal F_T$. The event proof works in discrete and continuous time; it says nothing by itself about expectations.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一滤过下逐路径 $S\\le T$，便有较早信息包含于较晚信息。事件证明适用于离散和连续时间，本身不保证期望等式。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000005",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[停止过程保持鞅|Stopped discrete-time martingale]]\n\nFor a real discrete-time martingale, $(M_{n\\wedge T})_{n\\ge0}$ is a martingale for every stopping time $T$, even if $T=\\infty$ is possible. Each fixed $n$ is finite.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实值离散鞅在任意停时下的停止过程仍为鞅，即使停时可能无穷。这里每个固定 $n$ 有限；尚未取随机终值。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000006",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 2380,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[一致可积|Uniform integrability]]\n\nOne cutoff makes every absolute tail expectation small; a small tail probability alone is insufficient.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n用同一个阈值控制整个族的大值加权贡献。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000009",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 2380,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[L1有界不推一致可积|L1 boundedness and UI]]\n\nRare spikes can keep a first moment bounded while moving all of it beyond each fixed cutoff.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n总一阶矩有界，仍可能把全部平均贡献推向越来越远的尾部。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000010",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2700,
      "y": 2380,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Lp有界推出一致可积|Higher-moment control]]\n\nA common $p>1$ and moment bound $C$ give a uniform tail bound $C/K^{p-1}$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n固定同一p>1及共同矩界；尾部界随阈值增大趋零。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000011",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 2380,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[一致可积与L1收敛|UI and L1 convergence]]\n\nGiven convergence in probability, UI is equivalent to an integrable limit and convergence in L1. Almost-sure convergence is a special case.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n依概率收敛配合UI，得到极限可积和平均绝对误差趋零。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000007",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 2860,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[可选停止条件|Optional stopping conditions]]\n\nDiscrete time: bounded $T$ preserves the mean. For a.s.-finite unbounded $T$, UI of $(M_{n\\wedge T})$ or one integrable envelope suffices. Finite $E[T]$ alone does not suffice.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n离散时间：有界停时保持期望。几乎必然有限但无界时，停止族一致可积或可积包络均是充分路线；仅 $E[T]<\\infty$ 不够。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103000000000008",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4500,
      "y": 2860,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[无限翻倍破坏可选停止|Doubling and optional stopping]]\n\nFair signs, unlimited stakes: $E[T]=2$ and $M_T=1$ a.s., but every finite stopped gain has mean zero. Rare large losses keep the stopped family from being UI.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n公平符号、无限下注模型中，$E[T]=2$ 且终值几乎必然为1，有限截断的期望却都是0。罕见大亏损使停止族不一致可积。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0013-l1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 3320,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[L1收敛|Convergence in L1]]\n\n$E|X_n-X|\\to0$ compares same-outcome errors and allows expectations to pass to the limit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n平均绝对误差趋零；不能用正负误差相互抵消代替。"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0015-cond-jensen",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[条件Jensen不等式|Conditional Jensen's inequality]]\n\nWith the same information $\\mathcal G$, integrable $X,\\varphi(X)$ and finite convex $\\varphi$ give $\\varphi(E[X\\mid\\mathcal G])\\le E[\\varphi(X)\\mid\\mathcal G]$ a.s.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n比较同一信息下的“均值的变换”与“变换的均值”。",
      "x": 4500,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 320
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
